n* **H. `parse_operation` input shape**: each of `+ * - / %` alone, several\n  together (fixed priority `+ * - / %`), none, empty, NULL.\n* **I. Operand value shape** for the five `*_op`: zero / positive / negative /\n  mixed signs / `INT_MIN` / `INT_MAX` / divisor `0` / divisor `-1`.\n* **J. `inreftree` param shape**, which selects the branches downstream:\n  `param2 == 0` (target reset 2→1) vs. `!= 0`; and\n  `tree_sum % 4` ∈ {0,1,2,3} (→ `+ * - %`) vs. {-1,-2,-3} (→ OOB `.rodata`\n  read). Note `'/'` is absent from `\"+*-%\"`, so `OP_DIVIDE` is unreachable\n  *via `inreftree`* and only reachable through the low-level entry points.\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table → exactly one feature configuration.\n\n## Rows (each = one meaningful combination; all randomized, seed-fixed)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | ✔ |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|---|\n| 1 | `add_op` | I: 0/±/mixed/`INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` + 20k random `(a,b)`; overflow wraps | [x] |\n| 2 | `multiply_op` | I: same, incl. overflowing products | [x] |\n| 3 | `subtract_op` | I: same, incl. `INT_MIN - 1` underflow | [x] |\n| 4 | `divide_op` | I: `b != 0`, both signs, `a=INT_MIN,b∈{1,2,-2}`, truncation toward zero | [x] |\n| 5 | `modulo_op` | I: `b != 0`, both signs, C truncating-remainder sign rule | [x] |\n| 6 | `find_node_by_id` + `node_table`/`node_count` writes | B/C: table seeded directly through the exported `node_table` symbol, `node_count` ∈ {0,1,7,49,50}; probe every id incl. absent ones. Compares the returned pointer **as an index into each library's own `node_table`** | [x] |\n| 7 | `add_tree_node` | D=`-1`, F=short label, from empty table → creates root, returns index 0 | [x] |\n| 8 | `add_tree_node` | D=existing parent, E=left free → links `left_child_id` | [x] |\n| 9 | `add_tree_node` | D=existing parent, E=left taken/right free → links `right_child_id` | [x] |\n|10 | `add_tree_node` | D=existing parent, E=both taken → node added, link dropped | [x] |\n|11 | `add_tree_node` | F: label 0/1/30/31/32/64 bytes + random high-bit bytes → full 32-byte `label` compared | [x] |\n|12 | `add_tree_node` | B: fill to `node_count == 49`, then 50th succeeds, 51st rejected | [x] |\n|13 | `add_tree_node` | random sequence of 200 `(id, value, parent_id, label)` ops incl. duplicate & missing parents; after every call compare full 2600-byte `node_table` + `node_count` + return value | [x] |\n|14 | `calculate_tree_sum` | C=single root, no children (`-1` sentinels) | [x] |\n|15 | `calculate_tree_sum` | C=root + left only / right only / both | [x] |\n|16 | `calculate_tree_sum` | C=3-deep left chain, and unbalanced deep chain (49 nodes) | [x] |\n|17 | `calculate_tree_sum` | C=dangling child ids + duplicate ids + values chosen to overflow | [x] |\n|18 | `calculate_tree_sum` | called on a **non-root** id (subtree sum), and on every id in a random tree | [x] |\n|19 | `parse_operation` | H: each single operator `+ * - / %` → 1,2,3,4,5 | [x] |\n|20 | `parse_operation` | H: multi-operator strings (all 120 permutations of `\"+*-/%\"`) → fixed priority | [x] |\n|21 | `parse_operation` | H: 5k random strings over a mixed alphabet (operators + letters + digits + high-bit bytes), plus embedded-NUL cases | [x] |\n|22 | `get_operation_func` | G: `op` = 1..5 → returned pointer must equal that library's own `*_op` symbol | [x] |\n|23 | `get_operation_func` → returned fn | G×I: call the returned pointer through FFI with random operands for every `op` in 1..5 | [x] |\n|24 | `inreftree` | J: `param2 != 0`, `tree_sum % 4 == 0` → `'+'` → `OP_ADD` | [x] |\n|25 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum % 4 == 1` → `'*'` → `OP_MULTIPLY` | [x] |\n|26 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum % 4 == 2` → `'-'` → `OP_SUBTRACT` | [x] |\n|27 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum % 4 == 3` → `'%'` → `OP_MODULO` | [x] |\n|28 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum % 4 ∈ {-1,-2,-3}` → OOB `op_string[-1..-3]` read | [x] |\n|29 | `inreftree` | J: `param2 == 0` (target reset) cros