→ `'-'` → `OP_SUBTRACT` | [x] |\n|27 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum % 4 == 3` → `'%'` → `OP_MODULO` | [x] |\n|28 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum % 4 ∈ {-1,-2,-3}` → OOB `op_string[-1..-3]` read | [x] |\n|29 | `inreftree` | J: `param2 == 0` (target reset) crossed with each `tree_sum % 4` residue | [x] |\n|30 | `inreftree` | J: `tree_sum == 0`, and `tree_sum` overflowing (`INT_MAX`-ish params) | [x] |\n|31 | `inreftree` | 100k random `(p1,p2,p3,p4)` incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` corners; also asserts the resulting `node_table`/`node_count` global state matches | [x] |\n|32 | `inreftree` | B: called with pre-corrupted `node_count`/`node_table`, then twice in a row (idempotence of the `node_count = 0` reset) | [x] |\n|33 | `node_table` / `node_count` (data symbols) | ABI: `sizeof(TreeNode) == 52`, array 2600 bytes, field offsets probed by writing through one library and reading field-by-field | [x] |\n\n## Binary executable\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` declares only `add_library(... SHARED src/lib.c)` — there\nis **no** `add_executable`, and the Rust `Cargo.toml` declares only\n`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` with no `[[bin]]`. So there is no driver binary and\nthe \"compare stdout byte-for-byte\" gate is **not applicable**; the differential\nharness compares return values and the full global-state bytes instead.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
