{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ijuyciohkrcbmb2b6tzr7vlklzyjjajs4ljbkmvc3j3xcbxsikoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Zero warnings/errors, `c_src/` untouched. Verification complete.\n\n## Result\n\n**One real bug found and fixed.** Everything else in the translation was already correct.\n\n### The bug: `divide_op` / `modulo_op` on `INT_MIN`\nBoth C functions guard only `b == 0`, not `INT_MIN / -1`. The C `.so` therefore dies with **SIGFPE (8)** on `idiv` overflow. The Rust used `wrapping_div`/`wrapping_rem`, which silently returned `INT_MIN` / `0`. Fixed by emitting a real `idiv` via inline asm on `x86_64`, so both now trap identically (verified: signal 8 in both; a negative control confirms the test catches the old code).\n\n### Phase artifacts (`translation/`)\n| File | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 13 C symbols (11 fn + `node_table`/`node_count`); `nm -D` diff **empty** |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **35 rows**, all `[x]`, + appendix on 2 API-unreachable UB conditions |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **33 rows**, all `[x]` |\n\n### Tests (`translation/tests/`, 74 total, all passing)\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` — the Rust crate is never linked directly, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are under test.\n\n- **Phase B** (33): every CONFIGS row, randomized with fixed seeds — 20k+ operand pairs per `*_op`, 100k random `inreftree` calls, all 120 operator permutations, plus the full 2600-byte `node_table` + `node_count` compared byte-for-byte after every mutating call.\n- **Phase C** (36): every ERRORS row asserts the *same* sentinel, not just \"both failed\". The 4 process-killing rows run in an identical **C host** (compiled at test time) so signals are comparable: `null_label`→11, `cycle`→11, `div_intmin`→8, `rem_intmin`→8, all matching.\n- **Phase D** (5): `nm -D` diff, undefined-symbol check, `RTLD_NOW` load, data-symbols-are-writable.\n\n### Notable C quirks confirmed replicated\n- `inreftree` indexes `op_string[tree_sum % 4]`, which goes **negative** for negative sums — an OOB `.rodata` read. Verified against the real C `.rodata`: `[-1]`=`\\0`, `[-2]`=`t`, `[-3]`=`f` (tail of `\"left-left\"`), all mapping to `OP_ADD`. The Rust's contiguous-literal blob reproduces this exactly.\n- `add_tree_node` scribbles `node_table[node_count]` *before* rejecting an unknown parent.\n- `parse_operation(NULL)` returns `OP_ADD`, not an error; priority is fixed `+ * - / %`, not left-to-right.\n- Out-of-range enum ints (incl. `0x10001`, `INT_MIN`) all fall to `add_op`.\n\n`./run_all.sh` automates the whole thing across both feature configurations (`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so default and `--no-default-features` are the complete space). Note it must build the cdylib explicitly — `cargo test` alone won't rebuild it, so the harness now hard-fails on a stale `.so`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2941,"cache_read_input_tokens":138895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2941,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"171ab39f-41d3-4216-89fa-31cd6b9d71c0","uuid":"4638c97d-b2c2-4a4e-91d6-d3ba187c6b8c","timestamp":"2026-09-05T14:55:03.509Z"}
